## 4. Functional Requirements

Applying the 5 Questions framework (**WHO? WHAT? WHEN? WHY? HOW WILL WE KNOW?**) to develop precise functional requirements.

| ID | Requirement | Source / Rationale | Verification Method |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **FR-01** | The system shall allow an authorized user to view equipment availability for a selected date range. | **Source:** Technician / Student need.<br>**Why:** To avoid booking conflicts. | **Test Case:** Search for an available item across specific dates and verify that returned availability matches database records. |
| **FR-02** | The system shall prevent a user from completing a booking request if the selected equipment is already reserved for any part of that time slot. | **Source:** Equipment Manager.<br>**Why:** To eliminate double-bookings. | **Test Case:** Attempt to book an already reserved item for overlapping hours; confirm the system blocks the transaction and displays an error message. |
| **FR-03** | The system shall record the exact date, time, and user ID when equipment is checked out and returned by a technician. | **Source:** Equipment Technician.<br>**Why:** To maintain accurate asset accountability and track overdue items. | **Test Case:** Perform a checkout and check-in operation; verify that audit logs correctly store timestamp and user ID. |

